  "stem": "In the equation \\(4(x + c) = 3x + 17\\), \\(c\\) is a constant. If the solution to the equation is \\(x = 2c - 1\\), what is the value of \\(c\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "3"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Distribute and solve for \\(x\\): \\(4x + 4c = 3x + 17\\), so \\(x = 17 - 4c\\).",
    "The solution is also \\(2c - 1\\), so \\(17 - 4c = 2c - 1\\).",
    "Then \\(18 = 6c\\) and \\(c = 3\\). (Check: \\(x = 5\\), and \\(4(5 + 3) = 32 = 3(5) + 17\\).)"
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "x, c = symbols('x c')\nxs = solve(Eq(4*(x + c), 3*x + 17), x)[0]\nsol = solve(Eq(xs, 2*c - 1), c)\nassert sol == [3]\nassert [Rational(a) for a in spr_answers] == sol",
